{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from the most incredible trip to Japan! It was a whirlwind of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and delicious food. Honestly, I'm already dreaming of going back.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Shibuya Crossing was an experience – a controlled chaos of people navigating the intersection. I spent hours exploring quirky shops in Harajuku and marveling at the vibrant street art in Shinjuku. The food scene was incredible, from Michelin-starred restaurants to tiny ramen shops tucked away in alleyways.\n\nNext up was Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan. Wandering through Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates was breathtaking. I visited serene Zen gardens, watched geishas gracefully glide through Gion, and learned about traditional tea ceremonies. The contrast between the modern energy of Tokyo and the historical charm of Kyoto was fascinating.\n\nBeyond the big cities, I took a day trip to Nara, where friendly deer roam freely in Nara Park. It was a truly magical experience!\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts, where ancient traditions seamlessly blend with cutting-edge technology. It’s a place that challenges your perceptions and leaves you with a deep appreciation for beauty and culture. Highly recommend adding it to your travel bucket list!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.25964632630348206}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -0.791698276